WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:13.465
woke up feeling miserable.

2
00:00:14.946 --> 00:00:17.767
She had a bad toothache and had not slept all night.

3
00:00:18.927 --> 00:00:24.489
She left for school in a bad mood, and when she arrived, the classroom was cold and smoky

4
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.390
because the fire wasn't burning well.

5
00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:30.292
The children were huddled around the stove, shivering.

6
00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:33.893
Anne sent her students to their desks.

7
00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:41.397
Later a student named Barbara Shaw came up to the blackboard to answer a math problem, and she

8
00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:42.818
tripped over the coal scuttle.

9
00:00:43.458 --> 00:00:45.559
Coal rolled to every part of the room.

10
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.763
When Barbara stood up, her face was covered in coal dust and the boys roared with laughter.

11
00:00:51.783 --> 00:01:00.588
"Really, Barbara," Anne said icily, "if you cannot move without falling over something, you'd better remain in your

12
00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:07.440
seat." As poor Barbara went back to her desk, her tears combined with the coal dust, producing a

13
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.521
truly grotesque effect on her cheeks.

14
00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:14.524
Then Anne caught Joe Sloane passing a small bag to Robert Brown.

15
00:01:15.585 --> 00:01:17.707
Anne guessed that the bag contained candy.

16
00:01:18.487 --> 00:01:22.170
She had warned her students before that candy in class would not be allowed.

17
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.513
And yet now Joe Sloane was passing candy against her explicit instructions!

18
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:33.052
"Joe," said Anne quietly, "bring that bag here."

19
00:01:33.853 --> 00:01:35.113
Startled, Joe obeyed.

20
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.754
"Now throw it into the fire," said Anne.

21
00:01:40.174 --> 00:01:41.675
Joe looked very scared.

22
00:01:41.695 --> 00:01:45.796
"P-please, Miss," he stammered.

23
00:01:45.816 --> 00:01:50.017
"Do what I say, Joe," Anne said sternly.

24
00:01:50.037 --> 00:01:55.179
"B-but they they're–" Joe said desperately.

25
00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:58.660
"Joe, are you going to obey me or not?"

26
00:01:59.160 --> 00:01:59.720
asked Anne.

27
00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:07.030
Finally, with an agonized glance at Robert Brown, Joe went to the fireplace and threw the bag in.

28
00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:14.432
For a few moments, Anne and the terrified students of Avonlea school did not know whether an earthquake

29
00:02:14.492 --> 00:02:15.992
or a volcano had hit them.

30
00:02:17.452 --> 00:02:23.934
The innocent-looking parcel, which Anne had thought contained candy, actually contained an assortment of firecrackers.

31
00:02:25.335 --> 00:02:30.076
The firecrackers exploded loudly, and sparks flew around the classroom.

32
00:02:31.044 --> 00:02:36.547
Anne sat down in her chair, pale, while all the girls climbed onto their desks shrieking.

33
00:02:37.808 --> 00:02:41.130
An hour later the fireworks were gone, and the room was tidied.

34
00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.911
Everyone was sitting quietly again.

35
00:02:45.072 --> 00:02:47.713
If Anne had been in a better mood, she might have laughed.

36
00:02:48.654 --> 00:02:51.195
Instead her mood had grown even worse.

37
00:02:52.876 --> 00:02:58.379
When Anne returned to the classroom after lunch, all the children were in their seats, studying, except for

38
00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:01.312
one—Anthony Pye.

39
00:03:01.332 --> 00:03:05.776
Anne opened her desk drawer to get some chalk, and a mouse leaped out and onto the floor.

40
00:03:05.796 --> 00:03:10.820
As Anne screamed and jumped, Anthony Pye laughed aloud.

41
00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:15.164
The mouse ran out the door, and the classroom was silent.

42
00:03:15.184 --> 00:03:18.807
"Who put that mouse in my desk?"

43
00:03:19.247 --> 00:03:19.847
asked Anne.

44
00:03:21.309 --> 00:03:26.032
Her voice was quite low, but it made a shiver go up and down Paul Irving's spine.

45
00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:32.857
She walked past Joe Sloane, who stuttered out wildly, "N-not m-me Teacher!"

46
00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:35.018
Anne paid no attention to Joe.

47
00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.601
She looked at Anthony Pye, and Anthony Pye looked back, unashamed.

48
00:03:40.621 --> 00:03:42.442
"Anthony, was it you?"

49
00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:43.542
asked Anne.

50
00:03:43.562 --> 00:03:46.944
"Yes, it was," he said insolently.

51
00:03:48.285 --> 00:03:49.926
Anne took her pointer from her desk.

52
00:03:50.746 --> 00:03:52.547
It was a long, heavy pointer.

53
00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.688
"Come here, Anthony."

54
00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:01.343
It was not the worst punishment Anthony had ever received, and Anne could never punish a child with

55
00:04:01.403 --> 00:04:03.964
cruelty. But the pointer did hurt a little.

56
00:04:04.685 --> 00:04:07.106
Anthony winced, and tears came to his eyes.

57
00:04:08.587 --> 00:04:13.069
Anne felt terrible, dropped the pointer, and told Anthony to go to his seat.

58
00:04:16.511 --> 00:04:17.812
Anne sat down at her desk.

59
00:04:18.912 --> 00:04:22.334
She felt ashamed and disappointed in herself for hitting a student.

60
00:04:23.715 --> 00:04:25.876
She had boasted that she would never do such a thing!

61
00:04:26.792 --> 00:04:28.513
How Jane Andrews would laugh at her!

62
00:04:29.474 --> 00:04:32.736
But worst of all, the students were looking at her with shock.

63
00:04:33.356 --> 00:04:35.657
And now Anthony Pye would never like her.

64
00:04:36.398 --> 00:04:38.959
She had tried hard to win his respect and love.

65
00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.922
That night at Green Gables, Anne cried in her bedroom with remorse.

66
00:04:44.662 --> 00:04:48.665
Marilla came in and exclaimed, "Why, Anne, what's the matter?"

67
00:04:48.685 --> 00:04:53.888
"Oh Marilla, I've had a terrible day," cried Anne.

68
00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.701
"At school today, I hit Anthony Pye for being naughty."

69
00:04:57.721 --> 00:05:01.943
"I'm glad to hear it," said Marilla.

70
00:05:01.963 --> 00:05:04.624
"You should have done it a long time ago!"

71
00:05:04.644 --> 00:05:07.085
"No, no, Marilla!"

72
00:05:07.465 --> 00:05:08.146
Anne cried.

73
00:05:08.166 --> 00:05:11.647
"You don't know how angry and mean I was.

74
00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:15.929
I can't forget the expression in Paul Irving's eyes.

75
00:05:16.989 --> 00:05:19.670
He looked so surprised and disappointed."

76
00:05:21.271 --> 00:05:24.505
Marilla stroked Anne's hair and said, "Never mind.

77
00:05:25.005 --> 00:05:26.186
We all make mistakes.

78
00:05:26.846 --> 00:05:30.009
This day's done and tomorrow is a new day."

79
00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:35.293
The next morning on the way to school, Anthony Pye met Anne in the lane.

80
00:05:35.313 --> 00:05:39.356
"Can I carry those books for you, Teacher?"

81
00:05:39.676 --> 00:05:40.256
he asked.

82
00:05:41.017 --> 00:05:42.338
Anne blinked in surprise.

83
00:05:43.219 --> 00:05:44.039
Was she awake?

84
00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:50.044
At school, when Anne took her books back from Anthony, she smiled at him, and he smiled back.

85
00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:54.415
From that day on, Anthony Pye's behavior was excellent.

86
00:05:57.077 --> 00:05:58.138
Later Mrs.

87
00:05:58.218 --> 00:06:02.402
Lynde said Anthony Pye had told his mother that Anne had "hit him like a man."

88
00:06:02.422 --> 00:06:07.746
"I never expected to get his respect by hitting him," said Anne.

89
00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:13.731
"My theory about kindness—that it's better than punishing students—can't be wrong."

90
00:06:13.751 --> 00:06:20.402
"No, but the Pyes are an exception to every rule," declared Mrs.
